Implementation Notes
--------------------

1. Routes code:

   Use JobDetails.js as model. This is after a lot of refactoring and extraction
   of boilerplate code into mainFunc.js. As we get time, we should update the old
   routes to the new model. Also the code generator in SQL can be updated to spit out
   the new format.

2. ToDo:

   TP_Todo.sql has table definitions.  TODO_ASSIGNABLE table not used. 
   Not needed. Can be accomplished with reusing TODO_ASSIGNMENT with TODO_id = 0


3. Chat:

   Uses websocket feature of express. Dumb implementation that simply rebroadcasts
   all messages received. The real smarts is in the Client only. Payload can be enhanced
   with advanced features such as DMs etc. Possible enhancement on server side is tracking
   user presence.

4. jobDetails.js:

   /getReleases query is heavily influenced from the legacy system. This is doing
   more than necessary and may be causing a slow down (legacy releases tab has a
   huge delay). We can pare down unused fields and joins when PO/SO order and
   Bill/Invoice features are completed.

5. Authentication & Authorization:

   No authorization is done on incoming requests. We can keep the service behind the
   firewall (port 3000 inaccessible from outside) and save the headache of authentication
   & authorization.

6. -
